{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1018","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1018","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1018\",\"parent_revision\":\"19f987740e600e2e6befcac38cd019bf9e1f362944bb7546cb183b8d410712e7\",\"root_revision\":\"19f987740e600e2e6befcac38cd019bf9e1f362944bb7546cb183b8d410712e7\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nrefresh_local_cache_from_github() takes 161 seconds to sync ~245 issues. The GraphQL migration (#916) changed transport from REST to GraphQL but did not optimize the query pattern \u2014 it may still be fetching issues one page at a time or making N+1 calls. The goal of the GraphQL migration was to reduce API round-trips, but the sync performance is unchanged or worse. Need to investigate the actual query pattern in operations.py refresh_local_cache_from_github and optimize to use bulk GraphQL queries (fetch all issues + labels + milestones in minimal round-trips).\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: Optimize backlog sync GraphQL query batching\\nGoal: Reduce refresh_local_cache_from_github() from 161s to under 10s by eliminating N+1 per-issue fetches.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. Current query pattern | AVAILABLE | Citation: groomer found N+1 pattern \u2014 2 bulk fetches then 245 per-issue pull_single_issue() calls\\n2. GitHub GraphQL pagination | AVAILABLE | Citation: _graphql_request_paginated uses cursor pagination, first:100\\n3. Max page size | AVAILABLE | Citation: GitHub GraphQL first:100 standard\\n4. Required fields per issue | AVAILABLE | Citation: _fetch_issues_graphql already returns labels, milestone, assignees, body\\n5. _fetch_issues_graphql signature | AVAILABLE | Citation: exists in github.py from T01\\n6. Test coverage | AVAILABLE | Citation: test_backlog_core_operations.py covers refresh\\n\\nAVAILABLE: 6, DERIVABLE: 0, MISSING: 0\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **backlog sync (refresh_local_cache_from_github) takes 161 seconds \u2014 optimize graphql query batching** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: User observation \u2014 session 2026-03-22, timed sync at 161.50s for 245 issues\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-03-22)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n**Command:** `time uv run python -c \\\"from backlog_core import models, operations; models.init(); operations.refresh_local_cache_from_github(output=None)\\\"`  \\n**Environment:** Local dev with network connectivity to GitHub API  \\n**Current measurement:** 161.50 seconds (observed 2026-03-22)  \\n**Issue count:** 245 total issues in repo\\n\\n### Scope\\n\\n**In scope:**  \\n- Restructure `refresh_local_cache_from_github` to fetch all issues+labels+milestone in one paginated GraphQL query per state  \\n- Eliminate per-issue `pull_single_issue()` loop from sync path  \\n- Reuse existing `_fetch_issues_graphql()` pagination infrastructure  \\n\\n**Out of scope:**  \\n- Changes to other sync operations  \\n- MCP server API changes  \\n- Changes to `pull_single_issue()` (used elsewhere)\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] `refresh_local_cache_from_github(output=None)` completes in under 10 seconds for 245 issues (161\u2192<10s)  \\n- [ ] GraphQL round-trip count is \u22645 (measured via mock call_count in tests):  \\n  - 1 call for OPEN issues (3 paginated pages @ 100 items/page = 1 initial + 2 follow-ups)  \\n  - 1 call for CLOSED issues (1-2 pages depending on count)  \\n  - 0 per-issue calls (eliminated N+1)  \\n- [ ] All existing tests in `test_backlog_core_operations.py` pass without modification  \\n- [ ] New test: verify `refresh_local_cache_from_github` makes exactly 2 _graphql_request calls (open + closed, no per-issue calls)  \\n- [ ] Backlog item cache is identical to pre-refactor (data equivalence verified)\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n**Primary:**  \\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py` (refresh_local_cache_from_github function)  \\n\\n**Secondary (tests/validation):**  \\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py` (test suite)  \\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/graphql_factories.py` (test mocks)  \\n\\n**Reference (no changes):**  \\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/github.py` (_fetch_issues_graphql \u2014 already bulk-capable)\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n**Build on:**  \\n- Existing `_fetch_issues_graphql()` with cursor pagination (2024, confirmed in codebase)  \\n- Existing `_graphql_request()` transport layer (phase 1, #773)  \\n- Issue#916 GraphQL batch infrastructure (confirmed available)  \\n\\n**Blocked by:** None identified\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\n**Estimated:** Low (2-4 hours)  \\n**Rationale:**  \\n- Single function refactor (refresh_local_cache_from_github, ~20 lines)  \\n- No new GraphQL infrastructure needed (existing _fetch_issues_graphql handles pagination)  \\n- Bulk GraphQL query already present and proven  \\n- Test updates: mock factory already supports pagination responses\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n**Producers:**  \\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py::refresh_local_cache_from_github` (primary change)  \\n\\n**Consumers:**  \\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py::backlog_list` (from_github=True flag)  \\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py` (mock tests for refresh_local_cache)  \\n\\n**Related infrastructure:**  \\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/github.py::_fetch_issues_graphql` (no changes needed \u2014 already supports bulk pagination)  \\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/github.py::_graphql_request` (transport layer, no changes)\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type:** Performance defect  \\n**Severity:** High \u2014 161 seconds for a single sync operation blocks downstream workflows  \\n**Root cause:** N+1 GraphQL query anti-pattern in `refresh_local_cache_from_github`\\n\\n## Artifact Manifest\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:begin -->\\n| Type | Path | Status | Agent | Created |\\n|------|------|--------|-------|---------|\\n| task-plan | plan/P1018-backlog-sync-n-plus-one.yaml | current | swarm-task-planner | 2026-03-24T16:16:09Z |\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:end -->\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"2cae6307c798642036208989d25136d3832188e47b4a768483eec0c196af1399\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVWXVsg\"}"}